From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: MAINTAINERS: classify KFENCE and KMSAN as MM components
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:30:41 -0800

Rename KFENCE to MEMORY MANAGEMENT - KFENCE and KMSAN to MEMORY MANAGEMENT
- KMSAN.  Move both entries to their alphabetical positions among MM
entries.

These entries cover the kernel heap fence detector and kernel memory
sanitizer.  Preserve every existing maintainer, reviewer, mailing list,
status and file pattern.

The following existing patterns move unchanged with each entry:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - KFENCE
        Documentation/dev-tools/kfence.rst
        arch/*/include/asm/kfence.h
        include/linux/kfence.h
        lib/Kconfig.kfence
        mm/kfence/

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - KMSAN
        Documentation/dev-tools/kmsan.rst
        arch/*/include/asm/kmsan.h
        arch/*/mm/kmsan_*
        include/linux/kmsan*.h
        lib/Kconfig.kmsan
        mm/kmsan/
        scripts/Makefile.kmsan

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Alexander Potapenko <glider@google.com>
Cc: Marco Elver <elver@google.com>
Cc: Dmitry Vyukov <dvyukov@google.com>
---

